.\" robodr-diode-unpack(1). Source of truth: the USAGE text in
.\" crates/robodr-diode/src/bin/robodr-diode-unpack.rs and the crate README.
.\" Keep them in sync.
.TH ROBODR\-DIODE\-UNPACK 1 "2026-10-16" "RoboDR 0.1.0-alpha.1" "RoboDR Manual"
.SH NAME
robodr\-diode\-unpack \- verify and import RoboDR export batches on the receiving (SOC) side
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robodr\-diode\-unpack
.B \-\-inbox
.I DIR
.B \-\-out
.I DIR
.B \-\-quarantine
.I DIR
.B \-\-processed
.I DIR
.B \-\-state
.I FILE
.B \-\-keyring
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-bundle\-key
.IR KEY_ID : HEX_KEY_FILE ]...
.RB [ \-\-partitions
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-accept\-gap
.IR UNIT : SEQ ]...
.RB [ \-\-max\-batch\-bytes
.IR N ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
High\-side importer of the RoboDR one\-way export
.RI ( robodr\-diode/1 ).
For every batch in the inbox it verifies the manifest signature with the
unit's key before parsing anything, checks the per\-unit sequence and hash
chain, the exact size and SHA\-256 of every file, re\-validates every finding
and parses every bundle (and verifies its signatures when a
.B \-\-bundle\-key
for its key id is given).
.PP
Accepted batches go to
.IR OUT / batch /records.jsonl
(one Kafka record per line) and then to the processed directory; duplicates
are recognised by hash and not re\-emitted; anything that fails a check goes
to the quarantine directory with a
.I .reason.json
file. A batch whose predecessors are missing is held in the inbox and
reported as a gap. Re\-running after a crash is idempotent. A JSON report is
printed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-inbox " DIR\fR, " \-\-out " DIR\fR, " \-\-quarantine " DIR\fR, " \-\-processed " DIR"
Where batches arrive, where accepted output is written, where rejected
batches are moved, and where imported batches are kept.
.TP
.BI \-\-state " FILE"
Importer state (per unit: last sequence, last hash, recent hashes, accepted
gaps), updated atomically.
.TP
.BI \-\-keyring " FILE"
One
.RI \(lq unit_id " " key_id " " hex\-key\-file \(rq
per line
.RB ( #
comments); relative key paths are resolved against the keyring's directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-bundle\-key " KEY_ID:HEX_KEY_FILE"
A black\-box key used to verify bundles signed with
.I KEY_ID
(repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-partitions " N"
Kafka partition count used to compute each record's partition.
.TP
.BI \-\-accept\-gap " UNIT:SEQ"
Accept batch
.I SEQ
of
.I UNIT
although earlier batches are missing (recorded in the state; the skipped
batches are refused afterwards). An operator decision.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-batch\-bytes " N"
Largest declared data per batch (default 256 MiB).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Everything was accepted or was a duplicate.
.TP
.B 1
Error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, including an argument that is not valid UTF\-8.
.TP
.B 3
Something was quarantined or held (gap).
.SH NOTES
HMAC\-SHA256 is a placeholder: the receiving side holds the same secret as
the unit and could forge batches.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR robodr\-diode\-pack (1),
.BR robodr\-blackbox (1),
/usr/share/doc/robodr/OPERATIONS.md
